==English==

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[separate]] and [[recover]] ([[valuable]] [[mineral]]s) by [[swirl]]ing dirt or crushed rock in a pan of water, in the manner of a traditional [[prospector]] seeking [[gold]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1907|author=w:Mark Twain|title=Chapters from My Autobiography|chapter=26
|passage=On the Saturday holidays in summer-time we used to borrow skiffs whose owners were not present and go down the river three miles to the cave hollow (Missourian for "valley"), and there we staked out claims and pretended to dig gold, '''panning out''' half a dollar a day at first.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1919|author=[[w:Gertrude Atherton|Gertrude Franklin Horn Atherton]]|title=The Avalanche|chapter=11
|passage=His father came out in '49 with the gold rush crowd, '''panned out''' a good pile, and then, liking the life—San Francisco was a gay little burg those days—opened one of the crack gambling houses down on the Old Plaza.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|figurative}} To [[proceed]] according to [[plan]]; to [[result]] or [[end up]] with an acceptable [[outcome]].
#: {{syn|en|shape up|work out}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1917|author=w:Mary Roberts Rinehart|title=Bab: A Sub-Deb|chapter=3
|passage=Many a pretty girl I have seen in my time, who didn't '''pan out''' according to specifications when I finally met her.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|year=1998|title=w:Friends|episode=The One With Rachel's Crush|role=w:Joey Tribbiani|passage=That was just a theory! There's a lot of theories that didn't '''pan out''': lone gunman, communism, geometry…}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=17 Oct 2004|author=Matthew Forney|title=Who's Getting It Right?|titleurl=https://archive.today/20130630104816/http://www.time.com/time/magazine/article/0,9171,725140,00.html?iid=digg_share|journal=Time
|passage=The China market is finally '''panning out''', thanks to the voracious consumerism of the middle class.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 July 29|title=Carne: "Treasury has its hands on the railway joystick already"|journal=Rail|page=9|text="It is anybody's guess how this is going to '''pan out'''. The Government will have even more control of the railway than before, with no incentive to innovate. [...]"}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2023-08-12|title=Harry Kane joins Bayern Munich and leaves door open for Spurs return|journal=w:The Guardian|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/aug/12/time-to-leave-harry-kane-signs-off-from-spurs-to-join-bayern-munich|passage=“It’s not a goodbye because you never know how things '''pan out''' in the future, but it’s a thank you and I’ll see you soon,” Kane posted on his social media accounts.}}

